      <section id="FuneralLimitations" class="content-section">
        <h2>What these funeral calculators can and cannot answer</h2>

        <p>
          These calculators can help organize cost categories, payment pressure,
          insurance gaps, savings impact, and debt tradeoffs. They cannot know a
          specific funeral home's price list, cemetery rules, state requirements,
          family wishes, religious practices, benefit timing, or every local fee. Use
          the result as a financial planning checkpoint, then confirm prices and terms
          directly with the funeral home, cemetery, crematory, insurer, or benefit
          administrator before committing.
        </p>

        <div class="funeral-hub-callout">
          <p>
            The safest funeral budget is the plan that honors the person while protecting
            the people left behind. If the plan requires high-interest debt, drains all
            emergency cash, or depends on money that has not arrived yet, resize the
            flexible choices before signing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

